# Furtive Courier: "can't be blocked as long as you've sacrificed an artifact this turn" and "Whenever this creature attacks, draw a card, then discard a card."
# (CR 509.1b, 611.3a, 701.21a, 701.9). Turn 1 Bot1 casts the Courier with three Moxes; turn 3 it plays its last card but the Black Lotus, casts and sacrifices
# the Lotus (an artifact) and attacks: Bot2's Grizzly Bears may not block it (the refusal). The hand is empty, so the loot draws the Mountain and
# then must discard it (discarding first would discard nothing): the Mountain is in the graveyard, not the hand.

